    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date feature for `POST /api/owners` (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since it's not in the `required` list it's optional on create, and because `Owner` is defined as `allOf: [OwnerFields, \u2026]` the field appears in both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`). `format: date` makes the generated field a `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column) with getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import. MapStruct maps it automatically in both directions (same name/type).\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** (the POST pipeline's build step) \u2014 After mapping the request to an `Owner`, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the client didn't supply one; a supplied date is preserved.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** for all four databases (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run against the `hsqldb` profile (`ddl-auto=none`), so the schema change is what actually lets the column persist.\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 `coreDefaultsToToday` (no date supplied \u2192 today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (`2020-06-15` echoed back) \u2014 both pass, and the full suite is green.",
